    "hook": {
      "text": "A mouse squeaks. A lion roars. You know which is which without being told, because one sound is high and the other is low. Press keys at different places on this keyboard. Can you find a squeak and a roar?",
      "exhibit": {
        "kind": "keyboard",
        "highlight": [],
        "low": "C3",
        "high": "C5"
      }
    },
    "explore": {
      "text": "Press keys all the way along the keyboard, from the far left to the far right. Listen to how the sound changes as you move.",
      "instrument": "keyboard",
      "exhibit": {
        "kind": "keyboard",
        "highlight": [],
        "low": "C3",
        "high": "C5"
      },
      "goal": "Play a key at the far left, then a key at the far right."
    },
    "name": {
      "cards": [
        {
          "text": "How high or low a sound is, is its [[pitch|pitch]]. A squeak has a [[high|high]] pitch. A roar has a [[low|low]] pitch."
        },
        {
          "text": "On a [[keyboard|keyboard]], low sounds are on the left and high sounds are on the right. Press the two glowing keys: the one on the left is low, the one on the right is high.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "C3",
              "C5"
            ],
            "low": "C3",
            "high": "C5"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "High does not mean loud, and low does not mean quiet. Pitch is only about how high or low a sound is, not how loud it is."
        }
      ],
      "alternative": {
        "text": "Think of instruments. A piccolo is tiny and sounds high, like a squeak. A tuba is huge and sounds low, like a roar. A violin sits in between. Small instruments tend to sound higher and big ones lower."
      }
    },
